    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="81977e77-a5bb-595c-a28d-9542fdcb8272" activityNameId="c35f517d-fe71-55b0-a0f6-78fe91da860b" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heat, residential, by combustion of synthetic natural gas from biological methanation using boiler, distrib [c7d0304f02]</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heat, residential, by combustion of synthetic natural gas from biological methanation using boiler, distributed by pipeline, produced by Electrolysis, PEM using electricity from grid and carbon sourced from DAC
This dataset represents the supply of 1 megajoule of heat in a residence, by synthetic natural gas from biological methanation combustion in a boiler.  The synthetic natural gas from biological methanation is produced by  Electrolysis, PEM, with electricity from grid as feedstock. The carbon is sourced from DAC. Heat conversion efficiency [% LHV input]: 109.5%. LHV [MJ/kg]: 48. Market price [Euro/MJ]: 0.03. Distribution loss [% output]: 0.02%. Storage loss [% output]: 0%. CO2 biogenic share [%]: 100%. Power [kW]: 16.4. Lifetime [years]: 20. Annual operation [hours]: 2100. : .  For more information, refer to: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023. Source: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023.

 UUID: 11f223a0-1b61-36e0-a813-09de8cb88191
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: Sampling procedure: Literature data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_11f223a0-1b61-36e0-a813-09de8cb88191.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
